plates-yolox-nano-256.onnx
  What: YOLOX-nano licence plate detector (one class), 1x3x256x256 BGR 0..255 without normalisation -> 1x1344x6 (x, y
        offsets and log width, height in grid cells, objectness and plate probability after sigmoid; anchors of strides
        8 / 16 / 32, row-major; decoded and suppressed in src/plates.rs). Plates are searched on square crops around
        YOLOX's vehicles (src/plates.rs `plate_crops`). Exported with torch.onnx.export (dynamo=False, opset 11, static,
        no decode), slimmed by onnxslim.
  Source: trained for this project, nothing to download. YOLOX 6ddff48 (Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX; patched: NMS without
          torchvision, torch.load weights_only=False, the export above) on torch 2.15, from Megvii's COCO checkpoint
          yolox_nano.pth: 150 epochs on the public crops with random down/up-scaling, blur and JPEG like the X5's; 40
          epochs with the first own tiles added, from its best checkpoint; 40 with the bike rides' added, from that
          one's best (AP 49.72, AP50 ~0.835, on a public validation slice of 1,149 crops; sha256 4408c8e9...); 40 with
          Vietnamese street photos added for two-line plates, from that one's best (AP 49.03 on the same slice; sha256
          57a8627e...); 40 with crops of the detection review added (hard negatives, below), from that one's best (AP
          49.58). Scripts, data and checkpoints are in target/plates-train and target/neg-scratch, not in git.
          sha256 ebada5d0f3ec33fc30d7f27e542bc464d15ff8f007c8fa5b0bc07161e2154562.
  Licence: YOLOX and its base weights Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Megvii Inc. -> LICENSE-yolox. No YOLOv9 code
           or weights in its line.
  Training data: 37,040 crops as `plate_crops` builds them, 31,620 boxes. Public, 22,660 crops: Open Images V7 "Vehicle
           registration plate" (8,157 images, 9,851 boxes; images CC BY 2.0, per-image attribution kept with the data),
           UC3M-LP (1,975 images; Zenodo record 17152029, CC BY 4.0), the Romanian licence plate dataset (534 images;
           RobertLucian/license-plate-dataset, MIT). Base weights: COCO 2017. Own X5 footage, 692 tiles repeated 10
           times: 392 with plates (445 boxes), 300 without, from 5 clips and 4 of the 5 bike rides, every tile reviewed
           by the user (17 rejected). Their boxes were judged by eye among candidates from the detectors at hand, the
           previous yolo-v9-t-256 included, or drawn by hand. The tiles are never in git. Two-line plates: 552 vehicle
           crops (733 plates) of 361 street photos of hoanglvuit/Vietnam_License_Plate_Segment_Datasets on Hugging Face
           (Vietnam; plate polygons, one-line and square two-line plates), repeated 5 times. **That dataset states no
           licence**, so its terms are unknown; the user chose to ship on 2026-11-09. Crops holding a confident box off
           the labelled plates were left out, as possibly unlabelled plates. The set's other half stays a test. The
           detection review: 470 crops of 22 segments of three bike rides, repeated 10 times: 82 around detections the
           user marked wrong (no label), 388 around plates the user confirmed (400 boxes); never in git.
